  "question": {
    "text": "Let $S$ be the set of all real values of $k$ for which the system of linear equations\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x+y+z=2 \\\\\n&2 x+y-z=3 \\\\\n&3 x+2 y+k z=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nhas a unique solution. Then $S$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dQ2bd",
      "text": "\nan empty set\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oX3w3",
      "text": "\nequal to $\\mathrm{R}-\\{0\\}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ijBxp",
      "text": "\nequal to $\\{0\\}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cZYfj",
      "text": "\nequal to $\\mathrm{R}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The system of linear equations is:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x+y+z=2 \\\\\n&2 x+y-z=3 \\\\\n&3 x+2 y+k z=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAs, system has unique solution.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\text { So, }\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n2 & 1 & -1 \\\\\n3 & 2 & k\n\\end{array}\\right| \\neq 0 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow k+2-(2 k+3)+1 \\neq 0 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow k \\neq 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence, $k \\in R-\\{0\\} \\equiv S$",
    "image": null
  },
